WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.770
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Writing Skills.

2
00:00:05.070 --> 00:00:08.561
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.861 --> 00:00:15.240
Unit fifteen: Problem and Solution. Today you will describe a problem and suggest solutions.

4
00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:18.297
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.233 --> 00:00:22.315
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.150 --> 00:00:23.919
Problem.

7
00:00:24.917 --> 00:00:27.334
Problem means something difficult to deal with.

8
00:00:27.950 --> 00:00:29.729
Traffic is a big problem.

9
00:00:30.317 --> 00:00:32.539
Your turn. Say: Problem.

10
00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:36.192
Problem.

11
00:00:36.950 --> 00:00:37.916
Solution.

12
00:00:38.917 --> 00:00:41.381
Solution means a way to solve a problem.

13
00:00:41.983 --> 00:00:44.041
One solution is more buses.

14
00:00:44.650 --> 00:00:47.268
Your turn. Say: Solution.

15
00:00:50.133 --> 00:00:51.134
Solution.

16
00:00:51.883 --> 00:00:52.826
Cause.

17
00:00:53.817 --> 00:00:56.327
Cause means the reason something happens.

18
00:00:56.917 --> 00:00:58.742
The cause is too many cars.

19
00:00:59.350 --> 00:01:01.410
Your turn. Say: Cause.

20
00:01:04.267 --> 00:01:05.303
Cause.

21
00:01:06.050 --> 00:01:06.889
Effect.

22
00:01:07.883 --> 00:01:09.953
Effect means the result of something.

23
00:01:10.550 --> 00:01:12.341
The effect is more pollution.

24
00:01:12.950 --> 00:01:15.440
Your turn. Say: Effect.

25
00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:19.150
Effect.

26
00:01:19.917 --> 00:01:20.918
Reduce.

27
00:01:21.917 --> 00:01:23.742
Reduce means to make smaller.

28
00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:26.083
Reduce the number of cars.

29
00:01:26.683 --> 00:01:29.138
Your turn. Say: Reduce.

30
00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:33.071
Reduce.

31
00:01:33.817 --> 00:01:34.899
Encourage.

32
00:01:35.883 --> 00:01:38.138
Encourage means to give support or hope.

33
00:01:38.750 --> 00:01:40.657
Encourage people to cycle.

34
00:01:41.250 --> 00:01:43.809
Your turn. Say: Encourage.

35
00:01:46.667 --> 00:01:47.749
Encourage.

36
00:01:48.483 --> 00:01:49.380
Implement.

37
00:01:50.383 --> 00:01:52.743
Implement means to put a plan into action.

38
00:01:53.350 --> 00:01:55.024
Implement a new policy.

39
00:01:55.617 --> 00:01:57.967
Your turn. Say: Implement.

40
00:02:00.833 --> 00:02:01.800
Implement.

41
00:02:02.550 --> 00:02:03.493
Suggest.

42
00:02:04.483 --> 00:02:06.576
Suggest means to offer an idea.

43
00:02:07.183 --> 00:02:09.287
I suggest building more bike lanes.

44
00:02:09.883 --> 00:02:12.396
Your turn. Say: Suggest.

45
00:02:15.233 --> 00:02:16.304
Suggest.

46
00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:20.913
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:21.750 --> 00:02:24.295
Visal, how do I write about a problem?

48
00:02:25.383 --> 00:02:33.852
First describe the problem and its causes and effects. Then suggest solutions and explain how each one helps.

49
00:02:34.950 --> 00:02:36.636
Which phrases can I use?

50
00:02:37.750 --> 00:02:46.138
Use one solution is, it would be helpful to and I suggest that. For example, I suggest that the city builds more bike lanes.

51
00:02:47.250 --> 00:02:48.286
How do I finish?

52
00:02:49.383 --> 00:02:55.704
Say which solution is the best and why. Show that the plan is realistic.

53
00:02:56.867 --> 00:02:58.692
Part three: grammar.

54
00:02:59.550 --> 00:03:02.444
Grammar focus: Suggesting solutions.

55
00:03:02.744 --> 00:03:03.965
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:04.650 --> 00:03:07.358
I suggest that the city builds more bike lanes.

57
00:03:08.250 --> 00:03:11.167
One solution is to reduce the number of cars.

58
00:03:12.133 --> 00:03:17.244
Use I suggest that, one solution is to and it would be helpful to when you propose solutions.

59
00:03:17.983 --> 00:03:21.704
Be careful! Don't say: I suggest that to build a lane.

60
00:03:23.667 --> 00:03:26.432
Say: I suggest that the city builds a lane.

61
00:03:26.732 --> 00:03:28.407
Use that plus a clause.

62
00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:31.957
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:32.767 --> 00:03:33.988
Fixing Traffic.

64
00:03:34.288 --> 00:03:36.857
Sovann writes about traffic in his city.

65
00:03:37.867 --> 00:03:40.749
The main cause is that too many people drive cars.

66
00:03:41.733 --> 00:03:44.488
The effect is air pollution and long delays.

67
00:03:45.500 --> 00:03:48.254
He suggests that the city builds more bike lanes.

68
00:03:49.267 --> 00:03:52.067
He believes this solution is realistic and cheap.

69
00:03:53.167 --> 00:03:57.076
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:03:57.917 --> 00:03:59.939
A solution solves a blank.

71
00:04:00.239 --> 00:04:03.649
A, problem. B, book. C, song.

72
00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:09.072
The answer is A: problem.

73
00:04:10.217 --> 00:04:12.495
A cause is the blank something happens.

74
00:04:12.795 --> 00:04:15.984
A, size. B, reason. C, price.

75
00:04:19.533 --> 00:04:21.382
The answer is B: reason.

76
00:04:22.517 --> 00:04:24.005
An effect is a blank.

77
00:04:24.305 --> 00:04:27.518
A, time. B, gift. C, result.

78
00:04:31.067 --> 00:04:33.391
The answer is C: result.

79
00:04:34.550 --> 00:04:36.317
Reduce means to make blank.

80
00:04:36.617 --> 00:04:39.586
A, smaller. B, bigger. C, wet.

81
00:04:43.133 --> 00:04:44.889
The answer is A: smaller.

82
00:04:46.050 --> 00:04:47.864
Sovann writes about blank.

83
00:04:48.164 --> 00:04:51.411
A, sport. B, traffic. C, music.

84
00:04:54.967 --> 00:04:57.198
The answer is B: traffic.

85
00:04:58.400 --> 00:05:01.308
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:02.150 --> 00:05:03.801
How do you write about a problem?

87
00:05:12.617 --> 00:05:14.105
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:14.405 --> 00:05:25.536
I describe the problem and its causes and effects. Then I suggest solutions with phrases like I suggest that. I explain which solution is best and why it is realistic.

89
00:05:25.836 --> 00:05:27.545
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:28.450 --> 00:05:32.913
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and suggesting solutions.

91
00:05:33.213 --> 00:05:38.060
Today's value is practical wisdom. Judge ideas by how well they work in real life.

92
00:05:38.360 --> 00:05:41.349
See you in Unit sixteen. Goodbye!

93
00:05:41.649 --> 00:05:44.325
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

